A||||1||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||Help! How do you remove a stripped wheel lock||||5||
Z||000000||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||12-26-2000||01:12 AM||||I have a 84 Fiero 2m4 with the 13" alloy wheels.  They came with a wheel lock that uses a ridge to twist the lug nut. <P>I have the tool for these locks, but on one of the special lug nuts the threads are bad.  I put the lug wrench on and start to torque, and the tool pops off.<P>Anybody know a way to remove the lug nut without damaging the stud?  My car is a rust free california car, I am certain the bolt will turn if I can get a wrench to stay on it.||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfixit58||12-26-2000||08:56 AM||||Use a cheap 12 point - 1/2" drive socket that is just one size too small to slide over the lug. Find a big hammer and drive it on. Then, just twist it off. After you get it off, it'll make you wonder just how secure your wheels really were.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
